build (:8097), same fixture data, for windows 2025-01 ($0.00, boundary),
2025-02 (-$4,537.30), 2025-09 ($422.06), 2025-11 ($3,007.98), and
2023-2025 (-$15,678.44, large negative). `diff` of the verdict-bar HTML
block showed the ONLY change in every case is removal of the old bespoke
button; the new KPI tile (fetched separately) rendered the IDENTICAL
formatMoney string and IDENTICAL sign class (positive/negative) in all
five cases. Both surfaces use one shared `formatMoney` (render.go:430,
single FuncMap entry) and the identical `ge $v.NetSavings 0.0` /
`ge .Metrics.NetSavings 0.0` condition on the same field
(verdict.go:176: `v.NetSavings = m.NetSavings`) — no dual-formatter risk.
Refund-dominant case is covered by the still-green
`TestVerdictBarNetSavings_MatchesSavingsModalTotal` (uses `refundRows()`,
asserts bar value == modal value and rejects a vacuous $0.00 fixture) —
`go test ./internal/handlers/dashboard/... -run NetSavings -v` PASS.

