Attack 3 (label truth): `internal/services/metrics/metrics.go:375-379`
computes `outflows := ts.FilterByType(models.Outflow)`;
`internal/models/transaction.go:13-26` defines `Transfer` as a TYPE
DISTINCT from `Outflow` with a doc comment confirming a Transfer row
"falls out of Total Income and Total Expenses" — so "transfers ... are
excluded" is true of the type contract. One-time-expense transactions
carry no separate ledger TransactionType (only Income/Outflow/Transfer
exist; OneTimeExpense is a What-If projection input) and the
metrics.go:370-372 comment confirms these three figures come "from the
FULL outflow set ... regardless of the flag" — so one-time IS included,
matching "all expenses" with no carve-out claimed. The keyword-inference
risk (a real transfer mistyped as Outflow) is a pre-existing
dataloader/classifier concern, not something this presentation-only task
could fix or that the label overclaims about — the label describes the
type contract, consistent with prior ruling guidance in the task brief.

